{"id":"word:hebrew:H8610","type":"word","title":"תָּפַשׂ","subtitle":"H8610 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to manipulate , i.e. seize ; chiefly to capture , wield , specifically, to overlay ; figuratively, to use unwarrantably","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to תָּפַשׂ (H8610) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 65 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"תָּפַשׂ (tâphas) means to manipulate , i.e. seize ; chiefly to capture , wield , specifically, to overlay ; figuratively, to use unwarrantably First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 11 30."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"תָּפַשׂ","transliteration":"tâphas","pronunciation":"taw-fas'","strong":"H8610","lemmaId":"hebrew:H8610","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["תֹּפְשֵׂ֣י","תִּפְשׂ֣וּ/ם","תָּפַ֛שׂ","וַֽ/יִּתְפְּשֵֽׂ/ם","וַֽ/יִּתְפְּשׂוּ֙"],"morphs":[["HVqrmpc",5],["HC/Vqw3ms",4],["HVqv2mp/Sp3mp",3],["HC/Vqw3mp",3],["HVNp3fs",3],["HC/Vqw3mp/Sp3mp",2],["HR/Vqc/Sp3mp",2],["HVqp3ms",2],["HC/Vqw3ms/Sp3mp",2],["HC/Vqrmsc",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to manipulate , i.e. seize ; chiefly to capture , wield , specifically, to overlay ; figuratively, to use unwarrantably","usage":"catch, handle, (lay, take) hold (on, over), stop, × surely, surprise, take.","full":"H8610. taphas תָּפַשׂ verb lay hold of, wield ( = Late Hebrew תָּפַם תָּפַשׂ, , Aramaic תְּפַם תְּפַשׂ, ); — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular ׳ת 2Kin 14:13 +, suffix consecutive וּתְפָשָׂהּ Deut 22:28 , etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִתְמּשֹׁ Isa 3:6 , 1 plural נִתְמְּשֵׂם 2Kin 7:12 , etc.; Imperative masculine plural תִּפְשׂוּ 1Kin 18:40 , etc.; Infinitive absolute תָּפשֹׁ Jer 34:3 ; construct תְּפשֹׁ Ezek 14:5 , לִתְמּשֹׁ 21:16 ; 30:21 , suffix לְתָפְשָׂהּ Deut 20:19 , etc.; Participle תֹּפֵשׂ Gen 4:21 +, construct תֹּפְשִׂי Jer 49:16 (Ges § 90l ), etc.; — 1 lay hold of, seize (with the hand), accusative of person, Gen 39:12 (J; + בְּבִגְדוֺ ), also ( ב person) Isa 3:6 ; Deut 21:19 ; Jer 37:14 ; Ezek 29:7 (in figurative; + ב instrumental); with ב of thing 1Kin 11:30 ; Deut 9:17 ; arrest, catch , accusative of person 1Sam 23:26 ; 1Kin 13:4 ; 18:40 (twice in verse); Jer 26:8 ; 37:13 ; 2Kin 14:13 2Chr 25:23 ; 2Kin 25:6 = Jer 52:9 ; Psa 71:11 ; in phrase catch, capture alive ( חַי ), accusative of person Josh 8:28 (JE), 1Sam 15:8 ; 1Kin 20:18 (twice in verse); 2Kin 7:12 ; 10:14 (twice in verse); seize city (accusative) Josh 8:8 (JE), 2Kin 14:7 ; 16:9 ; 18:13 = Isa 36:1 ; Deut 20:9 ; Jer 40:10 ; figurative Ezek 14:5 seize Israel (accusative) by ( ב ) their heart (terrorize them); Prov 30:9 seize (do violence to) the name (accusative) of my God; זָהָב תָּפוּשׂ Hab 2:19 grasped (sheathed) in gold ; ׳ת גִּבְעָה מְרוֺם Jer 49:16 holding (occupying) the height of the hill . 2 grasp in order to wield, wield, use skilfully : grasp sword בַּכָּף Ezek 21:16 (accusative omitted), compare 30:21 ( ב of sword), and especially participle: הַקֶּשֶׁת תִּפֵשׂ Amos 2:15 , כִנּוֺר תֹּפֵשׂ Gen 4:21 (J), ׳ת מַגָּל Jer 50:16 , מָגֵן תֹּפְשֵׂי 46:9 a (strike out ׳ת 46:9 b ᵐ5 Gie Co Du), ׳ת מָשׁוֺט Ezek 27:29 , חֲרָבוֺת 38:4 ; even ׳ת הַתּוֺרָה Jer 2:8 they that handle (deal with, are expert in) the law , ׳ת הַמִּלְחָמָה Num 31:27 (P) those skilled in war . — Jer 34:8 see below Niph`al Perfect 3masculine singular נִתְמַּשׂ Ezek 19:4 , 2 feminine singular נִתְמַּשְׂתְּ Jer 50:24 , etc.; Imperfect 3feminine singular וַתִּתָּפֵשׂ 51:41 , 2 masculine singular תִּתָּפֵשׂ 34:3 ; 38:23 , etc.; Infinitive construct לְהִתָּפֵשׂ Ezek 21:28 ; &#8212; be seized, arrested, caught (sometimes || נִלְכַּד ), subject person, Jer 38:23 ( ב instrumental), 50:24 (figurative of Babylonian ), also (with ב instrumental) Ezek 12:13 ; 17:20 ; 19:4 , 8 (both figurative of Israel), 21:29 , and (without ב ) 21:28 ; Num 5:13 ; + Infinitive absolute Qal תִּתָּפֵשׂ תָּפשֹׁ Jer 34:3 ; be seized , of fortress, city 48:41 (both || נִלְכַּד ), 50:46 , compare 51:32 ; figurative Psa 10:2 may they be caught in ( ב ) the devices which they have planned. Pi`el Imperfect 2masculine singular תְּתַמֵּשׂ Prov 30:28 a lizard thou mayest grasp with the hands ( ב ); — or read תִּתָּפֵשׂ Niph`al Imperfect 3 feminine singular, see De Toy. I. תֹּ֫פֶת see תוף .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 11 30","keyReferences":["1Kgs 11 30","1Kgs 13 4","1Kgs 18 40","1Kgs 18 40","1Kgs 20 18","1Kgs 20 18","1Sam 15 8","1Sam 23 26"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":65,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 11 30","book":"1Kgs","chapter":11,"verse":30,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּתְפֹּ֣שׂ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 13 4","book":"1Kgs","chapter":13,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִּפְשֻׂ֑/הוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqv2mp/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 18 40","book":"1Kgs","chapter":18,"verse":40,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִּפְשׂ֣וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqv2mp"},{"reference":"1Kgs 18 40","book":"1Kgs","chapter":18,"verse":40,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַֽ/יִּתְפְּשׂ֑וּ/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"1Kgs 20 18","book":"1Kgs","chapter":20,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִּפְשׂ֣וּ/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqv2mp/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"1Kgs 20 18","book":"1Kgs","chapter":20,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִּפְשֽׂוּ/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqv2mp/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"1Sam 15 8","book":"1Sam","chapter":15,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּתְפֹּ֛שׂ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 23 26","book":"1Sam","chapter":23,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/תָפְשָֽׂ/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vqc/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"2Chr 25 23","book":"2Chr","chapter":25,"verse":23,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תָּפַ֛שׂ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqp3ms"},{"ref